[gd_resource type="Theme" load_steps=14 format=3]

; Every control in the game pulls from this. Nothing should ever render in
; default Godot grey.
;
; Palette (M4.7): near-black slab, ONE AMBER PHOSPHOR accent, warm desaturated
; text. Square corners throughout — the UI is stencilled onto equipment, not a
; web page.
;
; The accent moved off ice-blue deliberately. Ice-blue is MOTHER's colour: it is
; what her inlays, her gates and her conduits are lit with. An interface in her
; colour reads as part of her system, and the player's interface is not — it is
; Northcairn-era human hardware, a phosphor tube, and the contrast between the
; two is load-bearing art direction rather than decoration. See UiFx's palette
; block and src/ui/crt.gdshader.
;
; The focus style is not cosmetic either. Every control in the menu is now
; focusable for controller navigation (MainMenu._wire_focus), so `focus` is a
; state a player will actually see — a bright amber bracket around whatever the
; stick last moved to, at a border width the hover state does not use, so
; "hovered" and "focused" can never be confused for each other.

[ext_resource type="Font" path="res://assets/fonts/ui_font_wide.tres" id="1_font"]

